			"Message": "docs(Grove): Expand README with comprehensive documentation\n\nMajor overhaul of the Grove README to improve developer onboarding and provide comprehensive documentation:\n\n- Add prominent feature description and Land ecosystem positioning\n- Add \"Key Features\" section highlighting WASM runtime, transport strategies, standalone operation, cross-platform support, VS Code API compatibility, and secure sandboxing\n- Add \"Core Architecture Principles\" table covering Security First, Transport Agnosticism, API Compatibility, Performance, and Composability\n- Add \"Grove in the Land Ecosystem\" table describing component roles (Extension Host Controller, WASM Runtime, Transport Layer, API Bridge, Activation Manager)\n- Add Mermaid architecture diagram showing Grove's internal structure and Mountain integration\n- Add \"Project Structure\" section with detailed directory tree\n- Add \"Deep Dive & Component Breakdown\" with links to key source directories\n- Add \"Getting Started\" section with prerequisites, build commands for native/WASM, feature flags, and usage examples\n- Add \"Security\" section documenting WASM sandboxing, memory limits, resource controls, type safety, and secure API\n- Add \"Compatibility\" section documentingCocoon, VS Code, and Mountain integration\n- Fix broken link from /why-wasm to /why-webassembly\n- Add \"Changelog\" section reference\n\nThis documentation refresh provides developers with a complete understanding of Grove's architecture, capabilities, and how to get started.",
