			"Message": "chore(Grove): Remove obsolete snake_case transport stubs\n\nDelete the old GrpcTransport.rs and IpcTransport.rs stub files that were redirecting to the canonical PascalCase modules (gRPCTransport and IPCTransport).\n\nThese stub files were kept temporarily during the PascalCase migration (commits 5b390de and c10204d) to maintain backward compatibility. Now that all consumers have been updated to use the new module names, the stubs can be safely removed.\n\nThis completes the transport layer cleanup following the PascalCase migration.",
			"SHA": "c3a3f0a24ffa42b4a737533cc02597808e2505a8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-04T08:20:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				73,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Grove): Complete transport layer PascalCase migration and extend languages API\n\nReplace old snake_case transport implementations with stubs redirecting to canonical modules:\n- GrpcTransport.rs → redirects to gRPCTransport (PascalCase gRPC acronym)\n- IpcTransport.rs → redirects to IPCTransport (PascalCase IPC acronym)\n\nExtend LanguageNamespace with full vscode.languages API surface:\n- Add 22 register*Provider methods: hover, definition, references, code actions, document highlights, symbols, workspace symbols, rename, formatting (document/range/on-type), signature help, code lens, folding ranges, selection ranges, semantic tokens, inlay hints, type hierarchy, call hierarchy, linked editing, declarations, implementations, type definitions\n- Add set_language_configuration method\n- Update doc comment to clarify these communicate with Mountain via transport layer\n\nThis completes the transport layer restructuring and brings the VS Code API compatibility layer to parity with the upstream vscode.languages namespace.",
			"SHA": "c10204d83e10ec16f6e5afe06ddc20443d77c1f4"
		}
